Chapter: VecLaneNegative
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A negative literal lane is refused by the other half of the guard, the one
 that compares against zero rather than against the lane count. It is a
 separate file from codex/test/errors/vec-lane-past-end.codex for that
 reason: neither can stand in for the other.

 This also pins that a negative literal reaches the check at all, which the
 first version of the check did NOT: a negative lane arrives as a unary
 negation wrapping the literal rather than as a literal, so `-1` compiled
 clean and emitted a binary while the zero-comparison arm sat unreachable.
 This file is what fires it.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (vec-extract (vec-splat 1.5) -1))
  end

